---
title: Jon's Christmas Muesli
author: Jonathan Simmonds
yields: 1%kg
cook time: 30 minutes
---

Combine @oats{500%g}, @macadamia nuts{100%g}(roughly chopped), @brazil nuts{100%g}(roughly chopped), @pumpkin seeds{50%g}, @muscovado sugar{50%g}, @mixed spice{1%tsp}, @cinnamon{1%tsp}, @ground ginger{1%tsp}, and @sea salt{1/2%tsp} together. Mix well.

Whisk together @water{180%ml}(boiling) and @muscovado sugar{50%g}. Add @walnut oil{60%ml} or @sesame oil{60%ml} and @vanilla extract{1/2%tsp}, then stir into the dry ingredients.

Spread the mixture into two large, shallow #roasting trays{}.

Toast at 170°C for ~{20-30%minutes}, stirring occasionally, until golden and crisp.

Stir in @dates{75%g}(chopped), @dried cranberries{75%g}, @mixed fruit{75%g}, and @crystallized ginger{50%g}(finely chopped).

> Add zest of 1 orange to the dry ingredients

> Substitute macadamia nuts for pecans
